# Delivery harness

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) before acting. It defines how work is selected, executed, and reviewed.

## Non-negotiable

- Implement only the story currently **In progress** on the board. Never two at once
- Test first. Watch it fail before writing the implementation (`tdd` skill)
- Branch per story, several small typed commits, PR to propose. Never commit on `main`
- **Never merge a pull request.** Open it, report status, and stop. Merging is a human action
- Run `npm run typecheck && npm run lint && npm test` before each code commit
- Log AI assistance with `scripts/ai_log.py` after the work

## Required process skills

`api-design` for endpoint changes, `architecture` for cross-module or storage changes, `security-review` for auth/URL/secret/limit changes, `code-review` before every PR, `pr-review` when reviewing one.

## Human approval

Every merge requires a human, without exception. URL allow/deny policy, authentication, cache invalidation, uniqueness handling, and the threat model additionally require the reviewer to confirm the design. Say so explicitly and wait.

## Never

- Fetch, resolve, or crawl a destination URL
- Use a 301 redirect; it is always 302
- Log raw API keys or raw IP addresses
- Weaken a test to make a build pass
- Add features the current story did not ask for
